#import "../template.typ": chapter, scenebreak

#chapter("CHAPTER ONE")

The typewriter sat on the desk like a relic from a forgotten age. Its keys, worn smooth by decades of rhythmic tapping, gleamed under the dim lamplight. John stared at the blank sheet of paper, the 1-inch margins staring back at him with an expectant silence.

He pressed the first key. *Clack.* The sound echoed through the small room, a sharp punctuation in the stillness. It was followed by another, and then another, until the room was filled with the frantic music of creation.

#scenebreak()

By midnight, the floor was littered with crumpled drafts. Each one represented a failed attempt to capture the essence of the story. But in the center of the desk, a single page remained—the first page of his new manuscript, formatted perfectly to the standards of the masters.

He leaned back, listening to the faint hum of the city outside, and smiled.
